From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: metadata writers, the stream provider of metadata handlers, Exif/GPS IFDs

Metadata handlers gain what Wine's conformance tests record from Windows (46
todo_wine marks removed from metadata.c):
 - IWICStreamProvider works: GetStream returns the stream the handler was loaded
   from unless WICPersistOptionNoCacheStream was given (WINCODEC_ERR_STREAMNOTAVAILABLE
   otherwise), GetPersistOptions and GetPreferredVendorGUID return what LoadEx got
   (the vendor defaults to Microsoft). LoadEx without a stream keeps the items.
   IPersist::GetClassID and IsDirty are real.
 - The writer classes exist for every reader (unknown, IFD, Exif, GPS, App1,
   PNG cHRM/gAMA/hIST/tEXt/tIME, GIF logical screen, image descriptor, graphic
   control, application extension, comment), registered as metadata writer
   components with IWICMetadataWriterInfo, along with the Exif, GPS and App1
   readers that had no class. A writer is the reader plus SetValue,
   SetValueByIndex, RemoveValue and RemoveValueByIndex, which replace a value of
   the same id, add a new one and mark the handler dirty.
 - IWICComponentFactory::CreateMetadataWriter makes a writer for a format (an
   unknown format gives the unknown writer unless FailUnknown; persist options are
   refused with E_INVALIDARG) and CreateMetadataWriterFromReader copies the items,
   the persist options, the vendor and a copy of the cached stream, converting
   nested readers to writers too.
 - An IFD holds its Exif (0x8769) and GPS (0x8825) pointers as readers of those
   IFDs, and the App1 item is the IFD number 0 as Windows has it (queries
   such as /app1/ifd/exif keep working).
Writing the items back to a stream (Save) is not done yet.
